# Design Tokens

## Source of truth
Use tokens from `shared/.../ui/theme/`:
- `VitranSpacing` — padding, gaps (`xs`…`xxxl`)
- `VitranSize` — icons, avatars, rails, touch targets, breakpoints
- `VitranRadius` — corner radii (also wired into `VitranShapes.material`)
- `VitranShapes.pill` — full-pill shape; `VitranShapes.material` — Material3 slots
- `VitranElevation` — shadow elevations
- `VitranOpacity` — alpha for inactive / muted chrome (`INACTIVE`)
- `VitranAnimation` — motion timings (e.g. `Tooltip.DURATION_MS`, `Tooltip.DISMISS_DELAY_MS`)

## Required
- Prefer tokens for spacing, icon/avatar sizes, radii, elevations, opacities, and shared layout sizes.
- Prefer `VitranAnimation` for shared tooltip / hover dismiss timings.
- Name by role/scale (`lg`, `iconMedium`), never by pixel (`spacing16`).

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
.padding(horizontal = 16.dp, vertical = 12.dp)
modifier.size(24.dp)
.shadow(elevation = 8.dp)
delay(80)

// ✅ GOOD
.padding(horizontal = VitranSpacing.lg, vertical = VitranSpacing.md)
modifier.size(VitranSize.iconMedium)
.shadow(elevation = VitranElevation.medium)
delay(VitranAnimation.Tooltip.DISMISS_DELAY_MS)
```

## When to add a new token
Add to the matching object **only if**:
1. The value is a normal scale step (or clearly reusable), **and**
2. You expect it on more than one screen/component.

Do **not** tokenize one-offs (e.g. `13.dp`, a single odd layout tweak, a one-off hover bridge).

## When not to tokenize
- Unique values used once
- One-off animation scales / spring params that are not shared
- Percentage-based shapes already covered by `VitranShapes.pill`

